WEBVTT

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.550
You may begin!

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.960
God, what a pain in the ass.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.100
Why do I have to take exams in a virtual reality?

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.090
It's a big waste of time!

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:52.490
Hey, pipe down, Sogoru!
You're disturbing the other students!

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.260
Right.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.810
Question!

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.510
What is it, Sogoru?

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:04.710
Problem number three. It can't be answered.

00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:06.620
Number three?

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:09.850
Oh yeah, I didn't cover that in class, did I?

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.020
Because it's a middle school-level problem!

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.990
I threw you guys a freebie.

00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:19.190
Don't tell me you can't figure it out!

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:25.320
Huh? Oh, is that what it is?!

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.400
Why can't I remember this?!

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.270
Come on!

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.140
I got nothing.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:46.860
Next..."Civilization." Bunmei... Bunmei...

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:47.950
Hey there!

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.230
You're working hard, huh?

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:52.960
Don't talk to me!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.720
Darn it, you're gonna knock all the
vocabulary I learned right out of my head!

00:02:58.530 --> 00:02:59.400
Oh...

00:02:59.730 --> 00:03:02.900
It's a little late to be pretending
you know your stuff.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.040
You seem pretty cocky, Kyo.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:08.510
Yup! I'm in top form right now!

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:10.210
These exams are a piece of cake!

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:15.920
See you, Kyo!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:16.750
Sure!

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.650
This is turning into a major operation.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:27.290
Still, if we destroy this, it'll make
our battles afterwards a lot easier.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.600
We can also hope to replenish
our current firepower.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:34.000
It might even tip the state of the war to our favor.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:38.500
He's counting his chickens
before they've hatched, isn't he?

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.940
It's all right. It looks like these
chickens will grow up just fine.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.050
With the firepower of three
Zegas attacking simultaneously,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.020
I believe our success is ensured.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.150
And if we fail with this much firepower,

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.380
it means we're doomed,
no matter what we try.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.510
What's Kyo's condition?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.420
He's recovered his specs to be
equal to all his previous versions.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:01.800
Equal to?

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.060
Yeah. Physically, he's a topnotch Gunner.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.000
We'll begin the operation
the day after tomorrow.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.010
Tarbo, get brushed up
on the plan, will you?

00:04:10.010 --> 00:04:11.240
Aye, sir.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:14.310
Equal to, huh?

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.240
Not the same, though.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:21.110
I could have gotten a perfect score if
not for that middle school question.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.790
Why couldn't I remember it?

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.690
You still doing this?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.930
You won't have much of a team if you
just get guys hoping to score with girls.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:35.460
Hayase, you're!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.260
What? You got a problem with this?

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:43.200
If I join, I can have this, right?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:44.670
Ushio!

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:48.380
I'm just living up to your expectations.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.210
You got more videos of Shizuno-sempai,
right? Copy 'em for me.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:57.890
What kinda team will we have
if you're just after chicks?!

00:04:57.890 --> 00:05:01.720
Don't give me that! We're friends, RIGHT?!

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:06.900
You got more footage, right?
The risqué stuff you cut out? Huh? C'mon!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.730
Like I'd have that?
Or at least, like I'd let you see it?!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.570
Oh, you little jerk! You're keeping
all the fun to yourself, huh?!

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.340
Naughty boy! We'll have to
confiscate that from you!

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:21.830
C'mon, we want it! Hand it over!

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.980
I have to practice a little.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:31.010
If I don't join the club, I'd be
here under false pretenses.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.550
ALL RIGHT!

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:41.020
Okay, now let me down. Let me down!

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.590
Right, right, right...

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.970
<i>Kyo, you're squeezing too hard!</i>
<i>Let me go!</i>

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.170
<i>No! I don't want to let you go.</i>

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:53.880
<i>Kaminagi...</i>

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:55.140
<i>No!</i>

00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:59.310
<i>I'm not lying! Kaminagi, I really do!</i>

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.150
<i>It's no use. See? You can't lie to me, Kyo.</i>

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.650
Idiot... It was nice.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:09.680
Even if it was a lie...

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.530
Our battles so far have mainly
been against patrols or ambushes.

00:06:17.530 --> 00:06:19.900
We've been merely reacting to attacks.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.630
However, this time we have our new members,
Chris and Arque, as well as Kyo Sogoru.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:25.870
Me?

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:31.850
As your battle skills have improved, you've
greatly enhanced the Oceanus' combat ability.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:34.540
Even as A.I.s, we're very happy about this!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:39.120
N-No kidding? Aw, it's not all that!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.350
So, am I a natural or what?

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:47.700
Now you can be proud to be a full-fledged
Cerebrant. Right, Miss Minato?

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.900
Huh? Oh! Right!

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.660
You're a fine Cerebrant, through and through!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:57.300
Wow, so does this mean I get promoted
from part-timer to full-time staff?

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.840
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:01.870
Sure!

00:07:04.410 --> 00:07:07.680
Now, to the task at hand.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:11.610
This is Oscar, a medium-scale deutera
zone located in the Pacific Ocean.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:14.990
As it is also the enemy's front line
base for the Far East battle front,

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:18.830
most of the enemy combat units
attacking the environs of Japan...

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.260
are believed to be launching from here.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.790
Our mission this time is to
attack Oscar... and destroy it!

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:33.710
If we stop Oscar's operations, we can step down
the defense condition of the Maihama server.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:37.640
However, just the fact it's an enemy
stronghold makes it very dangerous.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:43.140
Therefore, I want to ask you for your
consent before we carry out this mission.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:46.550
Consent? Oh, is that why you're
making the big show of flattering me?!

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:48.150
It's not like I'd turn it down!

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.230
He saw through it.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:52.160
I'm surprised he figured that much out.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.830
Fine! I'll do it!

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.990
However! I've got one condition!

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:00.930
Condition?

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:06.260
I want you to cancel the
shutdown of the swim club!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:16.110
I'll get the members I need! Please!
Just give me another month! I'm begging you!

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.850
Very well.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.510
I'll give you an extension till
the start of the next semester.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.690
All right! I'm holding you to that promise!

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:28.130
In exchange, I hold you
to showing us a success.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:33.220
Leave it to me! The pool will be
overflowing with members when I'm done!

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.640
Give me strength...

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.710
You sure you want to
make a promise like that?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:43.200
It's an easy condition to meet.
Besides, he's the one who made it.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.380
That's true, but...

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:50.410
It's not a lie. He can have an
extension to get more members.

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.340
You're cruel.

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.160
We're at war!

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.390
Say, Commander Shima...

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.430
What?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:08:59.920
We have a condition of our own.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:06.730
Extra dimensional adjustments, complete.

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:10.600
Cosmological constant control
values converging. Now stabilized.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.110
Well done.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.040
We managed the modification
this time with little trouble.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:20.710
Based on Shizuno's data from before, I optimized
the process to have minimal side effects.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:24.080
Carry on and assist with stabilizing Arque's data.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.980
Aye, sir.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.190
Later.

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.360
See you tomorrow.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:29.050
Sure!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:41.130
Why are they?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.280
Papa!

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:03.550
We just wanted a little time off.

00:10:03.730 --> 00:10:06.730
It's been ages since we've seen it rain.

00:10:06.730 --> 00:10:08.720
It'll make a nice memory.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.870
Memory?

00:10:10.870 --> 00:10:15.040
Yeah. We're remaking our memories.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:18.560
I've apparently lost quite a few of them.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:23.500
Well, that's not a good sign. You shouldn't
talk like someone who's about to die!

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.880
But, you see...

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.780
I <i>am</i> about to die.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:34.610
That's why I'm treasuring this time I have now.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.760
What kind of crap are you laying on me?!

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:41.530
We're just phantoms!
How can you be dying?!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:45.960
You still haven't recovered
completely, have you?

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.000
I see. Sorry. Just forget about it.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:52.630
Wait a second!
What are you talking about?!

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:57.550
Chris... Tell him.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.530
Arque!

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.020
Tell me what?

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.280
Kyo...

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:10.620
We're human data stored
completely on quantum computers.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.790
I understand all that.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.190
No, you don't understand.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:26.340
We're just masses of data, but the amount
of data that comprises us is enormous.

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:32.270
With that much data, a certain
amount of error always creeps in.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.280
What do you mean?

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.720
It's impossible to achieve a
100% perfect quantum teleport.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:44.410
Each time we entangle,
a tiny amount of data is lost.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:48.200
A special characteristic
of a quantum computer...

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:52.370
is that quantum teleportation doesn't leave
the original data behind after transmission.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.770
It's impossible to make
copies or backups.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:58.730
The system literally moves the original
data from one location to another.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:03.670
As a result, there's no way
to restore deleted data.

00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.520
Since a human body
follows a basic pattern,

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:13.080
you can use differential analysis
to reconstruct it to a certain point.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:18.590
However, if you lose what
makes a person an individual,

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:20.960
there's no recovery from that.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:22.900
What makes you an individual?

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:23.920
Memories.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.870
As you lose the memories
you compile over a lifetime,

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:31.900
your personality gradually
begins to change.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:34.740
You cease to be "you."

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:40.010
A while back, Arque suffered
a major transmission failure...

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:44.550
and took a lot of damage to both
her body and memory data.

00:12:44.550 --> 00:12:51.480
Even now, each time she quantum teleports,
her body is eaten away a bit more.

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.750
No way...

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:57.920
At least you still remember who I am!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:01.630
Of course I do.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.500
You understand, Kyo?

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.780
It's true that we're all just data.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:16.840
But that doesn't mean that we can't die.

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:22.850
<i>Don't be crazy. In a game, you just hit</i>
<i>the reset button and come back to life.</i>

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:30.890
<i>Is it possible that'll happen</i>
<i>to me too, some day?</i>

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.830
<i>No.</i>

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:36.900
<i>Or has it happened already?</i>

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.680
<i>Did I feel that sense of déjà vu...</i>

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:49.010
<i>because I was really seeing something</i>
<i>that had already happened before?</i>

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:55.110
<i>Is it possible I was</i>
<i>just not remembering it?</i>

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.190
<i>If that's true, then I'm also!</i>

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.890
Whatcha doing?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.490
You just need one more member?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:11.870
Good for you. It's all thanks to my
P.R. video. You should thank me!

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:14.710
Even though everyone ignored it?

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.580
So what? You can say it did, anyway.

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:21.010
That's just how these things work out.

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.450
So what if it's based around a lie?

00:14:24.450 --> 00:14:27.850
Maybe one day that lie
will become the truth.

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:32.020
<i>A lie can become the truth!</i>

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:40.060
You weren't serious before, were you?

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:48.080
Your mind was on a million
other things, wasn't it?

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:51.710
But, when you said you
didn't want to let go of me...

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:52.770
Yes!

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.040
I was totally thinking about
something else that time!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:05.990
Sorry about that!
Things just kinda got the better of me.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:08.620
I swear, that wasn't how I really felt!

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:12.100
Sorry! My bad! Please forgive me!

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:19.700
Kyo, you're a jerk!

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:27.970
We may just be data... But it hurts.

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:31.840
What the hell am I doing?

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:36.050
Am I really damaged? Or else?

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:44.400
<i>60 seconds to start of Oscar</i>
<i>destruction operation number three!</i>

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.430
<i>Zegapains, prepare for transmission.</i>

00:15:46.570 --> 00:15:50.370
<i>Bednorz parameters, stabilized!</i>
<i>Bednorz curve, holding!</i>

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.310
<i>Reconstruction coordinates, set and locked!</i>

00:15:52.670 --> 00:15:55.160
We're transmitting to the very edge of our range.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:57.210
<i>Altair, transmit!</i>

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.240
Entangle!

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:08.920
Transmission, complete. C.H.I.P.
loss within acceptable parameters.

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:12.090
Confirming transmission of
Garuda, Hraesvelg, and Caladrius.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:14.860
We've hit our target coordinates, as planned.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:17.760
Was the pain I feel
inside also "as planned?"

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:22.160
The damage level from teleporting...
It's not zero, is it?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.770
It's within acceptable limits.
Nothing that should cause an issue.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:29.270
But it's an issue for <i>me.</i>

00:16:30.040 --> 00:16:31.170
Who told you?

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.380
I could tell even without asking anyone.

00:16:34.380 --> 00:16:37.010
Are you trying to get me
to tell you something?

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.980
Is there something I should know?

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:44.190
Yes, you're right.
You were reborn once before.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.120
Thank you.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:50.330
Target, in sight!

00:16:52.600 --> 00:16:55.330
Zega team, approaching Oscar.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:00.240
Altair is leading, as planned.
Proceeding to probe its power.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.950
They've noticed me! Gimme some backup!

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:13.850
<i>Roger!</i>

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:31.870
Shit! I can't break through this thing!

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:34.610
It has a high barrier potential.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.370
Setting the tunneling coefficient of
the Ezaki perforator to maximum!

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.360
Beginning penetration!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:51.520
All right!

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.970
Outta my way!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.570
Multiple large vessels at 10 o'clock!

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:09.970
Viagems?!

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:14.300
They're still inactive!

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:28.190
All dressed up for us.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:30.390
Wow! They're totally exposed!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:32.700
Shall we?

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:34.290
Of course!

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.440
BONUS STAGE!

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:46.640
We are now ten minutes into the operation.

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.580
So, they've begun.

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:53.050
No way!

00:18:53.050 --> 00:18:55.490
One unit did all this?!

00:18:56.690 --> 00:19:00.250
Looks like our blitzkrieg went
completely according to plan.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:05.130
Where's the main force?!

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.500
Enemy squadron confirmed at 5 o'clock!

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.930
In short, there they are!

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:23.480
Altair is moving towards the core!

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:24.950
Moving to support!

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:25.350
Roger!

00:19:29.160 --> 00:19:30.220
We're heading in, too!

00:19:30.220 --> 00:19:30.850
Right!

00:19:37.770 --> 00:19:42.170
What's got you so excited, Kyo?
Did your girlfriend dump you?

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:44.870
I'm just making sure of something.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:48.140
That right now... It's "me" who's here!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:58.910
Sempai! What was I like before it happened?!

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:02.620
What's the point of asking?

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:06.020
What did I do when things got tough for me?

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:10.930
You held everything that bothered you inside.

00:20:10.930 --> 00:20:13.200
Took on the entire burden of fighting...

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:18.170
And you ended up... destroying yourself.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:24.100
THEN TO HELL WITH THAT GUY!

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.360
No response from Oscar!

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:44.520
Zega team losses: zero!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.930
Zegatank! Resupply Q.L. to all units!

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:49.930
Bring us into transmission
range and recover them at once!

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:09.380
Yeah... Definitely hurts.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:17.960
<i>Who cares? I'm a new man now!</i>

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:53.790
And so, the end of the world drew close.

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:56.660
Our tomorrows became a dream.

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:59.270
Making memories was meaningless.

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:02.470
Even so, I'll document the real world.

00:23:02.470 --> 00:23:04.960
Until the moment the world ends...

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:09.310
But what is real? What's real and what's a lie?

00:23:09.310 --> 00:23:11.000
I want to know!

00:23:11.850 --> 00:23:15.010
Next time, on Zegapain:
"Again, Summer Comes."

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:18.650
My thoughts, never to be erased.
